# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
build/
dist/

# Virtualenv -- the model weights alone are 4.5 GB
.venv/
venv/

# Logs from installs and spikes
*.log

# The eval screens and the annotated figures ARE committed. They are every one of them
# drawn by evalset/screens.py and evalset/hard_screens.py, so they are reproducible --
# but a judge cloning this repo should be able to see what the benchmark was measured
# against without running anything first. evalset/out/NOTES.md states plainly that they
# are synthetic.
#
# No images in the repository.
#
# Every evaluation screen is DRAWN by evalset/screens.py and hard_screens.py, so the
# benchmark is reproducible from source without shipping a single PNG -- and a repo that
# never carries an image cannot accidentally carry a screenshot of somebody's screen.
# README step 11 has the two commands that regenerate them.
*.png
*.jpg
*.jpeg
*.gif
*.webp
*.bmp

# One exception: the architecture diagram, because a README that explains a privacy tool
# should show its trust boundary rather than describe it. It is drawn by
# docs/make_architecture.py and contains no screen content, so none of the reasoning
# above applies to it.
!docs/architecture.png

# Scratch output from a local run is not committed.
#
# The prefixed patterns below are not tidiness, they are a near miss. A spike run over a
# real capture wrote `evalset/out/_small_source.png` -- an UNREDACTED copy of a
# screenshot with a live API key in it -- into this directory, untracked but not
# ignored. Exactly the same way the keys CSV nearly went public earlier. Research scripts
# that take a real image as input must not leave their intermediates somewhere a
# `git add .` can reach.
evalset/out/_scratch*
evalset/out/*.redacted.png
evalset/out/_verify_*
evalset/out/_cell_*
evalset/out/_vs_*
evalset/out/_aws*
evalset/out/_mesh_*
evalset/out/_grid_*
evalset/out/_small_*
evalset/out/_quota_*
evalset/out/_probe_*

# Benchmark output is committed on purpose -- it is evidence. Uncomment to exclude.
# evalset/results.json

# Never commit a real screenshot or capture to this repository.
*.capture.png
captures/

# Real credentials. A keys CSV was found sitting in this folder, untracked but not
# ignored -- one `git add .` away from being public. These patterns are deliberately
# broad: the cost of ignoring a file you wanted is a minute, the cost of publishing a
# key is an incident.
*accessKeys*
*access_keys*
*credentials*
*.csv
*.pem
*.key
*.pfx
*.p12
.env
.env.*
*.env
secrets.*
*_rsa
*_ed25519
id_rsa*

# The quarantine folder, wherever someone points it.
quarantine/
snapguard-quarantine/
.snapguard/
